@startuml possession-flow-rotation
' ⚠ A DETAIL DIAGRAM. The whole possession, and the second-chance LOOP, are in
' possession-flow.puml — read that first. This step runs BETWEEN possessions,
' OUTSIDE that loop.
' ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS: the three substitution tiers, and the technical-foul roll.
' ⚠ Notes say what the flow DOES; the argument lives in possession-flow-model.md.
' Render: plantuml -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=16384 -tpng   (every diagram is now under
'   the 4096px default, so the flag is insurance — but keep using it, and ⚠ keep each
'   diagram SCREEN-SIZED: past ~2,000px it stops being readable long before it stops
'   rendering. ⚠ `-checkonly` does not lay out and does not catch deprecated syntax
'   that renders as a warning box — look at the PNG.)
title RotationState — between-possession substitution\n//§3.5 fatigue · §3.13 foul trouble · §3.14a technicals//

skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteFontSize 10

start
:drain on-floor energy (× endurance)
recover benched energy;

if (**technical foul?**\n//P = TECHNICAL_FOULS_PER_TEAM_GAME ÷ nominal checks//\n//rolled PER TEAM, no causal model at all//) then (yes)
  :FOUL — TECHNICAL_FOUL
  committer: //foulProne//-weighted draw
  over the ON-FLOOR FIVE only
  **own counter** — not foul-out, not foul-trouble, not bonus;
  :**1 free throw** to the other team
  shooter = highest //freeThrows// on the floor
  (DETERMINISTIC — consumes no RNG);
  note right
    A technical hangs off no contest, so it is rolled HERE,
    between possessions, and not on the possession path.
     **The possession is UNCHANGED** — no fork, no retention,
    no switch, even when the offense commits it.
  end note
else (no)
endif

:**hard** — force off any fouled-out OR ejected player
//isFouledOut() || isEjected() || isEjectedForFlagrant()//
//(fouls >= 6 · technicalFouls >= 2 · flagrantTwos >= 1)//
→ sub from full roster;
:**soft** — foul-trouble sub
//P = base(fouls) × subAggressiveness × value × roster//
from //rotationDepth// window only; yields if bench can't cover;
:fatigue sub — pull most-tired starter below
//subAggressiveness// threshold for freshest bench
within //rotationDepth//; starters pulled later / return first;
note right
  Three tiers: **hard/forced · soft/preference · fatigue**.
  Ejection extends the HARD tier via the `eligible(...)`
  filter — NOT a fourth removal path. Disqualification is
  always **DERIVED** from monotonic counters.
  ⚠ **Consumes THREE RNG draws** — the sit roll, the technical
  roll and the committer draw — ALL taken unconditionally at
  fixed points, even when unneeded, so the stream never forks
  on rotation state.
  The step emits no events: it RETURNS the technical's
  committer; PossessionEngine emits the FOUL + free throw.
  The soft rule protects the BEST players MORE — the deliberate
  inverse of the fatigue rule's starter tolerance. Sticky sit:
  return is EARNED via the fatigue freshness path, never
  re-rolled. onFloor() is always exactly 5. A fouled-out
  player NEVER returns.
end note

:→ the possession begins
//possession-flow.puml//;
stop
@enduml
